restart: always
Docker restarts the container if it crashes/fails OR stops.

1. Application crashes
Container running
      ↓
Application crashes
      ↓
Container stops
      ↓
Docker restarts it ✅
2. Container stops normally
Container running
      ↓
Container stops
      ↓
Docker restarts it ✅
3. You manually stop it
docker stop mycontainer
Even if the container was stopped manually, Docker's restart behavior can cause it to be started again when the Docker daemon/Compose-managed setup is brought back.

Use this when you want a service to continuously stay running.



